GitCric — third-party notices
=============================

GitCric is distributed under the MIT License (see LICENSE). It includes
third-party work as described below.

GitCric's GitHub-user scoring engine is derived from GitFut and reuses a
substantial portion of its scoring math: the GitHub signal set, the six-axis
raw-stat mapping, the within-profile z-score → tension-pair → spike pipeline,
the role-weighted OVR, and the two-band (stats cap + legacy gate) OVR
structure. The axes were re-mapped from football to cricket and the
calibration constants have since been refitted, but the structure and much of
the code originate there.

Derived files:
  web/lib/scoring/        (engine.ts, constants.ts, types.ts)
  web/scripts/gitfut-ref.ts   — a direct port, retained as a calibration
                                reference with GitFut's original constants

